# SideX desktop app — optional environment overrides.
#
# None of this is required. SideX runs with no account and no configuration:
# it starts its own agent server on loopback and reads whatever provider
# credentials you already have. Set things here only to override that.

# ── Provider keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any of these that are already exported in your shell are picked up
# automatically. You can also enter keys in Settings → Models, which takes
# precedence over the environment. See src-tauri/src/commands/providers.rs
# for the full provider catalog and resolution order.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# ZHIPU_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# ── Local models ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp and vLLM are detected automatically on their
# default loopback ports (11434, 1234, 8080, 8000 respectively). To point at
# a different host or port, set the base URL for that provider in
# Settings → Models instead of here — the app resolves it fresh from there
# each time it starts the agent server, so an env var of the same name set
# in this file would just be overwritten.

# ── Agent server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app builds and supervises `sidex-server` itself. Point at your own build
# or a server you started by hand if you'd rather manage it yourself.
#
# SIDEX_SERVER_BIN=/path/to/sidex-server

# Display name shown in the chat UI's local profile. Defaults to your OS
# username. There is no SideX account behind it.
# SIDEX_USER_NAME=

# ── Remote semantic index (optional, off by default) ─────────────────────────
# Search is on-device BM25 unless you point this at a service you run.
# SIDEX_CLOUD_API=
